{
  "_": "money's screenshots (.github/screens/apps.md; which phones it is on is flake.nix's list, `publish`): its server is server.sh, seeded up to the run's day (DEMO_DAY), signed in to as `user`, who goes by `name`. `walk`: the phones' and the larger screens' (each a list), walked inside the app from a new install (ui/docs/shots.md, \"In the App\"): `welcome`, the first run's page a new install opens on; then signed in through the first run (Get Started, the server's address typed — `{server}` is the run's — Continue), landing on the budget; and every shot after reached by tapping from where the last left it, each its steps' labels as the views on the screen say them (a shot's `<id>.tree.txt`). `touch`: once the walk is over, the one real tap on each phone's screen (XCUITest's on the iPhone, `adb input` on Android), the app's ready signal after it. Each stop is taken in the theme the walk is in, the theme switched, and taken again. A category and a transaction are opened in the platform's way: on a phone Category Details' sheet and the transaction's form; on a larger screen the inspector (Transaction Details shown first). `desktop` is the iced window's (ui/rust/shots): its size, and its shots, each clicking what a text on the screen says, in one window. Its accounts are Checking's register, its transactions all accounts'. `screens` and `launch` are the Mac's and the browser's: each screen opened by its launch arguments (the Mac's own window, app-mac.sh; the browser's address, app-web.sh), as no walk takes them.",
