  "_screens": "`screens`: the Mac's and the browser's, each screen opened by its launch arguments alone (ark_app::shell::Launch: .github/screens/apps.md) on the sizes it is `on` (`mac`, and the browser's `ios`, `ipad-portrait`, `ipad-landscape`), under one id on all of them, the same ids as the walk's. A category and a transaction are two entries, one id: on the larger sizes in the inspector (`-inspector 1`), on a phone's as the platform shows them. The Mac takes them but for the menu and the pages: it has no step driver and no fresh launch, and no browser to sign it in, so `launch.mac` opens the demo's household before each (at 1440x900), on the run's day (app-mac.sh gives `-demo` DEMO_DAY), the same household the server is seeded with.",
  "launch": {
    "mac": [
      "-demo",
      "2026-11-18",
      "-window",
      "1440x900",
      "-ApplePersistenceIgnoreState",
      "YES"
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "id": "budget",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "budget"
      ],
      "route": "/budget",
      "on": [
        "ios",
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape",
        "mac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "category",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "category:dining"
      ],
      "route": "/category/dining",
      "on": [
        "ios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "category",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "category:dining",
        "-inspector",
        "1"
      ],
      "route": "/category/dining?inspector=1",
      "on": [
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape",
        "mac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "accounts",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "accounts"
      ],
      "route": "/accounts",
      "on": [
        "ios",
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape",
        "mac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "account",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "account:checking"
      ],
      "route": "/account/checking",
      "on": [
        "ios",
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape",
        "mac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "review",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "review"
      ],
      "route": "/inbox",
      "on": [
        "ios",
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape",
        "mac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "transaction",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "transaction:receipt"
      ],
      "route": "/transaction/receipt",
      "on": [
        "ios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "transaction",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "transaction:receipt",
        "-inspector",
        "1"
      ],
      "route": "/transaction/receipt?inspector=1",
      "on": [
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape",
        "mac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "add-transaction",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "add-transaction"
      ],
      "route": "/transactions?sheet=new-transaction",
      "on": [
        "ios",
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape",
        "mac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "insights",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "insights"
      ],
      "route": "/insights",
      "on": [
        "ios",
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape",
        "mac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "settings",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "settings"
      ],
      "route": "/settings",
      "on": [
        "ios",
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape",
        "mac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-assign-menu",
      "args": [
        "-screen",
        "budget"
      ],
      "route": "/budget",
      "steps": [
        {
          "tap": "Auto-Assign",
          "role": "button",
          "where": "bottom",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "wait": 1
        }
      ],
      "on": [
        "ios",
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "welcome",
      "fresh": true,
      "route": "welcome/",
      "on": [
        "ios",
        "ipad-portrait",
        "ipad-landscape"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "web": {
    "_": "The browser's (app-web.sh, web-shots.js): money-web over the demo household in the page (`query`'s `demo`: no server to sign in to) seeded to `today`, at each of `sizes` (named as `screens`' `on`) in light and dark. Every one of `screens` is taken on the sizes it is `on`, its launch arguments as the page's address (`-screen budget` is `?screen=budget`); `shots` are the browser's own besides, on every size unless they say: the transient parts, each opened by its address — arkui-web's `context` (a row's menu), `menu` (a control's), `popover` (a field's), `command` (the command box), `keys` (the keys panel) — then its steps in the desktop's vocabulary (click, key, type, await, wait).",
